Gizmo the Gnome Warlock cackled as his Succubus, Vexa, lashed out at a Stranglethorn tiger. "Beautiful chaos!" he cheered, dodging a swipe. But then, a group of Horde rogues ambushed them from the jungle foliage. Gizmo panicked, reaching for his fear spell, but Vexa was already ahead. She didn't just attack; she charmed the lead rogue, turning him against his own friends. Amidst the confusion, Gizmo realized why he rarely saw other warlocks with her. While Vexa was a powerhouse, her most famous ability often caused more trouble than it solved in crowded areas, leading many to prefer the stoic, predictable Voidwalker instead.

**Answer:** The Succubus's **Seduction** (or Charm) ability frequently causes pets to break crowd control or pull extra mobs unintentionally in group settings or crowded quest hubs, making the Voidwalker's reliable **Torment** (taunt) and durability a safer, more socially acceptable choice for general play despite the Succubus's higher damage output. [end of text]


